### 4. What was the rule of Bluetooth, and should we remove it?

**What it did originally**:
In the decompiled original PlayCulture APK, Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) was used as an offline beacon to trigger "proximity infection" when two phones were ~10–20 meters apart without relying on GPS accuracy.

**Why removing it is the right move**:
- **OEM Battery Killers**: Aggressive battery managers on Redmi/Xiaomi (MIUI/HyperOS) and OnePlus (OxygenOS) frequently kill background BLE scanning, causing missed tags.
- **Hardware Variation**: Bluetooth antenna signal attenuation (phone in pocket vs. case) causes wildly erratic distance estimations (a phone 2m away can read as 25m away).
- **Permission Fatigue**: BLE requires continuous runtime Bluetooth/Nearby Device permissions that often get revoked.

**Conclusion**: Removing Bluetooth and replacing it with the **5-meter / 10-second GPS chase rule** makes the game vastly more accurate, reliable, and fair across all phone models.

