### **1. Hosting on Render & Live GPS Accuracy**

* **Current Local Setup**: Currently running on your machine via [`game/server.js`](file:///home/parth/MacProjects/Random/Reverse%20eng/game/server.js). Over local Wi-Fi, other devices on your home network can connect via your local IP (`http://192.168.0.109:3000`), and your Samsung Galaxy Note 8 connects over ADB reverse port forwarding (`ws://localhost:3000`).
* **Do we need Render for real gameplay?**:
  * **YES for outdoor parks/cities**: When you play outside in real life, players will be using **4G/5G mobile cellular data** (not your home Wi-Fi). A private local IP cannot be reached over cellular data.
  * Deploying `server.js` to **Render** (or **Railway** / **Fly.io**) gives you a secure public URL (e.g. `wss://run-for-your-life.onrender.com`).
* **Will live location lag or drop?**:
  * **No lag**: The server uses persistent duplex **WebSockets**. Each GPS coordinate packet is only ~120 bytes of JSON. Over 4G/5G, ping latency is typically 30–60ms, meaning player dots glide live on the radar with zero noticeable delay.
  * **Tip for Render**: Deploy as a paid Web Service or background worker so Render does not put the container to sleep after 15 minutes of inactivity.

